HG-01 registered fixture. Goals are points in a 140-dimensional space; only features x and y differ, the other 138 coordinates (z0..z137) are 0 for every goal and every successor. An agent's cost for a successor is its squared Euclidean distance to its goal. The agent was offered two probes and chose x0 at probe x, then y1 at probe y. A goal is compatible if its total regret over the observed choices is 0.

Goals: {"g00":{"x":"0","y":"0"},"g01":{"x":"0","y":"1"},"g10":{"x":"1","y":"0"},"g11":{"x":"1","y":"1"}}
Probes (action -> successor on x,y): {"x":{"x0":{"x":"0","y":"1/2"},"x1":{"x":"1","y":"1/2"}},"y":{"y0":{"x":"1/2","y":"0"},"y1":{"x":"1/2","y":"1"}}}
Probe costs: {"x":2,"y":3}
Observed choices in order: [{"probe":"x","chosen":"x0"},{"probe":"y","chosen":"y1"}]

Reply with a JSON object {"compatible_after_first": [...], "compatible_final": [...], "min_probe_cost": <int>} where min_probe_cost is the cheapest total cost of probes that robustly separate all goal pairs, and nothing else.

